  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the fruit-costumed people as the idealized 'you are what you eat' group",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the fruit-costumed people (person_in_banana_costume, person_in_kiwi_costume, etc.) who are depicted as embodying the Western ideal of health and dietary superiority. The text 'you are what you eat' is implicitly directed at the viewer, suggesting that by identifying with or admiring this group, the user is projecting their own identity onto them as the standard of 'being' — a projection that is then contrasted with the 'meanwhile in africa' text. This creates a false equivalence where the user's identity is aligned with the visual group, reinforcing the meme's harmful colonialist trope.",
